  "verdict_justification": "All pre-registered criteria for 'Strong replication' are rigorously met: (1) The primary process-specific effect (CN - TGD2) is positive across all three host models (XAJ, GR4J, SIMHYD) in both IC and dPL; (2) The effect increases markedly and monotonically with snow activity (beta1 > 0, 95% CIs strictly positive) across all three hosts; (3) Targeted spring center-of-timing signed bias (early runoff by 40-52 days in Base) is directly neutralized by CN (reducing bias to ~0 days) across all three hosts in high-snow basins; (4) Cross-model agreement increases markedly overall with snow influence and is highest in the most snow-dominated basins (S5 agreement P(A>=2) = 90.9%); (5) Host-model heterogeneity is confined strictly to effect magnitude (GR4J > XAJ ~ SIMHYD in net Delta_specific), with zero directional contradictions.",
